# Queue Requirements

## Scope
FIFO queue system for Sanity CMS basket reservation requests (create, rollback, realize) to prevent race conditions. Sequential processing, atomic operations, persistence, idempotency, concurrency control, retry logic, circuit breaker.

## Out of Scope
Multiple queue instances, extra test/verification queues, payment processing (only stock decrement on payment success), UI blocking logic implementation, CMS schema changes.

## Definition of Done
[ ] Single production queue (no other instances), 0 cost, runs 24/7
[ ] INPUT: basket reservation requests stream, OUTPUT: queued, one at a time, atomic (waiting for 1 request to finish 100% before starting next), stream of basket reservation requests to sanity CMS, passing sanity reservation basket back to ui
[ ] Sequential FIFO processing, atomic operations:
    - Means: One request at a time via processQueue() while loop, priority queue first then normal queue, DB transaction wraps entire request operation (trx() - either all succeed or all fail)
    - Human verification: Add TRACE logs at processQueue() entry, transaction start, transaction commit/rollback, request complete. Send 3 requests rapidly, check logs show sequential processing (request 1 complete before request 2 starts), verify transaction boundaries, confirm no overlapping processing
[ ] Priority queue: realize requests before regular requests
[ ] Idempotency: UUIDv4 key, fingerprint, 24h CMS cache
[ ] Fingerprint: prevents malicious same idempotency key request attempts, 24h CMS cache TTL along with idempotency key
[ ] Concurrency control: one operation per reservation token
[ ] Retry logic: create (3x), rollback (10x), transient vs non-transient
[ ] Circuit breaker: open after 5 failures, 30s cooldown
